invariant: INV-50
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh sha512_compress_blocks_advancing
reason: the third of eight_rounds_advancing's eight rounds names the
  working variables at f and g in each other's roles, so Ch takes them in
  the wrong order in rounds 18, 26 and every eighth round after, and
  every digest is wrong. The call still names eight distinct variables,
  so nothing but the value shows it. The advancing harness holds the
  eight rounds to FIPS 180-4's own eight over every input, and its
  assertion on e to h fails.

--- old
    one_round(v->g, v->h, &v->b, v->c, v->d, v->e, &v->f, x, k[2] + next_word(ring, i + 2));
--- new
    one_round(v->g, v->h, &v->b, v->c, v->e, v->d, &v->f, x, k[2] + next_word(ring, i + 2));
